emises set out during uh  the campaign her significant focus is  about growing the economy we can't just  have a managed decline that won't help  anybody and that is why in terms of  getting growth going really matters both  uh in terms of making sure that we focus  on making it easier to do business and  that is why i'm really excited by the  appointments that we have  in the chancellor in business in trade  but this is a cross-government effort  and we will continue to make sure that  we do strain every sinew pull every  lever that we can in order to get our  economy growing again  as i say we cannot just look forward to  manage decline and liz has got i think  the bold economic plan to make sure that  we can get on and deliver that  nobody said this is going to be easy  we're conscious that around the world we  have an inflationary challenge  i'm conscious that we will continue to  keep our commitments uh to honor and to  continue to support ukraine as they are  part of this uh unnecessary aggressive  act of um war by putin on ukraine so  there's a number of challenges of course  that this government is facing today  we're not alone in that in terms of uh  global issues but we am determined sorry  i'm determined that we will support the  prime minister and we will on the plan  that she's setting out in order to make  sure that we can grow the economy that  we fix the energy challenge and that we  make sure that we uh tackle the backlogs  and also access to primary care  now of course i appreciate of your time  this morning race coffee but just a  couple more questions if you if you will  um  about abortion there have been concerns  raised about your  voting record about abortion and do you  personally support it  um i'm conscious i have voted against  abortion laws  what i will say is i'm the complete  democrat and that is done  so it's not that i'm seeking to undo  any um any aspects of abortion laws  yeah i mean just and just to follow up  on that then i mean  